-- title:
--   Inertia degree along the β-leg is one over ̄ k
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ and $s$ be non-zero natural numbers and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field. Inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k$ consider the level-$M$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldC k M`, the $k$-subfield generated by the $q$-expansions $j(q)$ and $j(q^M)$, and the roof `charLDegeneracyRoof k M s`, the $k$-subfield generated by $j(q)$, $j(q^M)$, $j(q^s)$ and $j(q^{Ms})$. The $k$-algebra map `heckeBetaC k M s` from the former to the latter is induced by the substitution $q \mapsto q^{s}$ on Laurent series, i.e. by the exponent-rescaling ring homomorphism `qExpand k s`. Assume `HeckeBetaCIntegral k M s`, that is, the underlying ring homomorphism of `heckeBetaC k M s` is integral, and let $W$ be a place of the roof over $k$: a proper valuation subring of the roof which is a principal ideal ring and contains the image of $k$. Then the inertia degree of $W$ along `heckeBetaC k M s` is $1$: viewing the roof as an algebra over `modularFunctionFieldC k M` through this map, the residue field of $W$ has degree $1$ over the residue field of the place of `modularFunctionFieldC k M` obtained by restricting $W$.
--
--   This is the statement that the residue extension at every place of the degeneracy roof is trivial along the $\beta$-degeneracy leg when the constant field is algebraically closed, so that in the fundamental identity $\sum e f = \deg$ only ramification indices contribute; it is the companion of the corresponding assertion for the $\alpha$-leg. It is used in the computation of place widths and of the Hecke correspondence on the roof in characteristic $\ell$, namely by [`ModularCurve.placeWidthChar_mul_correspondence_heckeBetaC_heckeAlphaC_single_apply_eq_of_prime_of_five_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.placeWidthChar_mul_correspondence_heckeBetaC_heckeAlphaC_single_apply_eq_of_prime_of_five_le) and [`ModularCurve.placeWidthChar_mul_correspondence_heckeAlphaC_heckeBetaC_single_comm_of_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.placeWidthChar_mul_correspondence_heckeAlphaC_heckeBetaC_single_comm_of_prime).
